  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDAAS (Ethiopian Digital Agriculture Advisory programme) - Improving Agricultural Advisory in Ethiopia through Digital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDAAS is a joint investment between the FCDO and the Bill &amp; Melinda Gates Foundation (BMGF) into a consortium led by Digital Green. The consortium works in partnership with the Government of Ethiopia (GoE) to deliver digital agriculture advisory services for farmers in Ethiopia through video-based and interactive voice recording channels. A key component of EDAAS is the development of an open-source, peer-to-peer data transfer platform called FarmStack for the secure transfer of data across public and private actors in the food and agriculture sector.</narrative>
  </description>
